    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0f45b1b8-8ac4-5dad-8415-b6599c16ee3d",
      ":question/problem": "Using the fact that\n\n$$\n75^\\circ=300^\\circ-225^\\circ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the **exact** value of $\\cos\\left(75^\\circ\\right)$.\n\n$\\cos\\left(75^\\circ\\right)=$ {{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(x-y)=\\cos x\\cos y+\\sin x\\sin y.\n$$\n\nApply it to the decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(75^\\circ\\right)=\\cos\\left(300^\\circ-225^\\circ\\right).\n$$\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(300^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(225^\\circ\\right)+\\sin\\left(300^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(225^\\circ\\right)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed special-angle values and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\right)+\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} \\\\\n&=\\frac{- \\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6}}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
