      ":question/problem": "Using the fact that\n\n$$\n285^\\circ=60^\\circ+225^\\circ,\n$$\n\ncalculate the **exact** value of $\\cos\\left(285^\\circ\\right)$.\n\n$\\cos\\left(285^\\circ\\right)=$ {{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the sum formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(x+y)=\\cos x\\cos y-\\sin x\\sin y.\n$$\n\nApply it to the decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(285^\\circ\\right)=\\cos\\left(60^\\circ+225^\\circ\\right).\n$$\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(60^\\circ\\right)\\cos\\left(225^\\circ\\right)-\\sin\\left(60^\\circ\\right)\\sin\\left(225^\\circ\\right)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed special-angle values and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\frac{- \\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6}}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
